# weft-board — design-system decisions

Fifteen decisions about what the `weft-board` template contributes to Weft and what it should hand back to existing primitives. **Every image below is a real side-by-side**: the left column is the existing Weft primitive rendered from `src/ui/*.tsx`, the right column is what the template introduces.

**How to use this doc.** Each item ends with a **Decision** line. Comment on that line to record the call — a plain "yes" adopts the recommendation, or say what you want instead. Resolve the comment when it is settled. Nothing here is applied to the code yet; these are proposals with the evidence attached.

Where a claim says *Measured*, it came from computed geometry in a live browser, not from reading the CSS. One of those measurements reversed my own earlier recommendation (see D4).

What is being proposed, in short:

- **Adopt an existing primitive, delete the template's version:** D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D6, D9, D10, D11
- **Promote something new into Weft:** D12, D13, D14
- **Split — existing visual, new meaning:** D7, D8, D15

---

## Group A — pure duplication (recommend: adopt the existing primitive)

### D1 · Action row — `weft-board-item` vs `HudListRow`

![Action row — `weft-board-item` vs `HudListRow`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** Same anatomy — title stack, sub line, trailing chips. `HudListRow` is the richer one: it carries state accents (unread / overdue / resolved / active) and density variants the template has no equivalent for, and it already backs SignalRow and ticket updates.

**Recommendation (superseded).** Adopt `HudListRow`; delete `weft-board-item`.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — reversed.** *"Update the weft version to what was introduced. It has better hierarchy."* `HudListRow` adopts the template's hierarchy; the template does not defer to `HudListRow`. State accents and density variants are retained.

**Decision (D1) — comment on this line to record the call.**

---

### D2 · Compact panel row — `weft-board-panel-row` vs `StatRow`

![Compact panel row — `weft-board-panel-row` vs `StatRow`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** Label-left / value-right, identical role. The only delta is the template's leading status dot, which `StatRow` has no slot for.

**Recommendation.** Adopt `StatRow`; add a leading slot for the status dot.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie).** *"Add the new version as a variant option."* The board treatment lands as an additive `StatRow` variant (leading dot slot + denser rhythm) behind a variant prop; today's appearance stays the default.

**Decision (D2) — comment on this line to record the call.**

---

### D3 · Drawer actions — `weft-board-drawer-actions` vs `ActionButtonRow`

![Drawer actions — `weft-board-drawer-actions` vs `ActionButtonRow`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** Same grouped-actions container. `ActionButtonRow` already supports start / end / between alignment; the template hard-codes the link button to `margin-left:auto`.

**Recommendation (superseded).** Adopt `ActionButtonRow`; delete the template's row.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — reversed.** *"The weft board drawer action should be the new pattern for ActionButtonRow."* `ActionButtonRow` moves to the template's arrangement (dense row, primary + default, link auto-pushed to the end).

**Decision (D3) — comment on this line to record the call.**

