## Group B — introduces a variant (decide: adopt, or promote the variant)

### D4 · Buttons — `weft-board-btn` vs `Button`

![Buttons — `weft-board-btn` vs `Button`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** **Measured: `Button size="sm"` is 32px; the template's is 33px.** The density rationale for a separate button does not survive measurement. The only real deltas are type size (14px to 12.5px) and radius (4px to 2px).

**Recommendation.** Delete `weft-board-btn`; use `Button size="sm"`. If 12.5px type and 2px radius are wanted, add them as a variant on `Button`.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — as recommended.** Buttons become `Button size="sm"`; the dense type/radius land as a `Button` variant. Reconciles with D3: the template wins on the row's *arrangement*, Weft wins on the *control* inside it.

**Link variant shown on request 2026-07-29.** Every variant × size that exists today, then the drawer's actual action row built only from existing `Button`, then the board's other link-styled contexts.

![D4 — Weft Button coverage including the link variant](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Verdict: the button use cases are covered, with one caveat and one gap.**

- **Covered.** `link` exists (`src/ui/button.tsx:22` — `text-primary`, `underline-offset-4`, underline on hover, no border or fill). Six variants × three text sizes plus `icon`. The drawer's row — primary, secondary, trailing link — needs no template-local button; the link is pushed to the end by `ActionButtonRow align="between"`, which is D3's layout decision, not a button concern. The board's three other link-styled controls (toast retry, reference-list *more*, menu items) are all covered.
- **Caveat (a11y).** A link-styled *button* is not a link. Keep these as `<button>` for actions and reserve `<a>` for navigation, or screen readers announce the wrong role. The Copy control deliberately uses `outline`, not `link` — it is an action with feedback, not navigation.
- **Gap (the usual one).** The plain-CSS layer has only `.weft-btn` and `.is-ghost` — no link, no outline, no size scale. That is precisely why the template invented `.weft-board-btn.is-link`. A single `.weft-btn.is-link` closes it; added to the cross-cutting widen-the-CSS-layer list.

**Decision (D4) — comment on this line to record the call.**

---

### D5 · Count / space chips — vs `Badge`

![Count / space chips — vs `Badge`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** `Badge` ships 5 tones and 4 variants. The template's three chips are a fixed outline pill, a fixed ink-tint, and a fixed danger outline — strictly narrower than what already exists.

**Recommendation (superseded).** Adopt `Badge`; delete all three template chips.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — reversed.** *"The introduced versions are more readable. I would like to keep them."* The count / space / status chips keep the introduced treatment. Landing them as `Badge` variants (not board-local) so future panels inherit them — same shape as D2. See D6: only the mono type chip moves to `SourcePill`.

**Decision (D5) — comment on this line to record the call.**

---

### D6 · Mono chip — `weft-board-type` vs `SourcePill`

![Mono chip — `weft-board-type` vs `SourcePill`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** **Measured: `SourcePill` is 16px tall / 10px type; the template's chip is 19px tall / 9.5px type** — smaller text in a taller chip, i.e. just more padding. `SourcePill` also has truncation and a muted tone the template lacks.

**Recommendation.** Adopt `SourcePill`; delete `weft-board-type`.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — as recommended.** *"Adopt source pill."* Brings truncation and a muted tone the template chip lacked. Paired with D5 — only this mono chip moves; the other chips keep the introduced treatment.

**Decision (D6) — comment on this line to record the call.**

---

### D7 · Segmented toggle — `weft-board-seg` vs `PillToggleGroup`

![Segmented toggle — `weft-board-seg` vs `PillToggleGroup`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** This is a real visual difference: Weft's CSS layer only has the gap-separated pill group. The joined segmented look (shared border, inset ring) exists in React as `ToggleGroup` but has no CSS-layer equivalent.

**Recommendation.** Keep the joined look, but land it as a plain-CSS counterpart of `ToggleGroup` rather than a board-local class.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — as recommended, sharpened.** *"Add the introduced visual as a variant of what already exists in weft."* A `joined` variant on `ToggleGroup` plus its plain-CSS counterpart; `PillToggleGroup` stays the gap-separated default.

**Decision (D7) — comment on this line to record the call.**

---

### D8 · Hint / provenance band — vs `Callout`

![Hint / provenance band — vs `Callout`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** `Callout` already covers this with 5 tones, an icon slot, an action slot and a title. The template introduces only two visual treatments Callout lacks: a dashed muted box and a filled footer band.

**Recommendation (superseded).** Adopt `Callout` for the hint. Decide whether the dashed and filled-band treatments become Callout variants or are dropped.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — reversed.** *"Adopt introduced UI."* Both treatments kept, landing as `Callout` variants (dashed, band) with Callout's current appearance as the default.

**Decision (D8) — comment on this line to record the call.**

---

### D9 · Error / empty — `weft-board-notice` vs `EmptyState`

![Error / empty — `weft-board-notice` vs `EmptyState`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** `EmptyState` is centered with an icon and action slot; the template's notice is a left-aligned dashed strip. Different shape, same job — keeping both means two answers to one question.

**Recommendation (superseded).** Pick one shape. Recommend `EmptyState` and delete the notice.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — reversed.** *"The new standard should be the UI that was introduced."* **Blast radius flagged:** `EmptyState` is consumed by Knowledge Search, Notes and other list panels for true empty states. Default reading pending confirmation — the introduced treatment becomes standard for **load-failure / notice** states while the centered icon+action shape stays for genuine empties, i.e. `EmptyState` gains the notice treatment rather than being replaced wholesale.

**Decision (D9) — comment on this line to record the call.**

---

### D10 · Panel header — `weft-board-head` vs `PanelHeader`

![Panel header — `weft-board-head` vs `PanelHeader`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** Same slots (title + actions + dismiss). The template's title is 19px/600 against `PanelHeader`'s HUD-dense strip — a larger board-scale header is the only thing introduced.

**Recommendation.** Adopt `PanelHeader`; if a board-scale title size is wanted, add it as a size variant.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — as recommended.** *"Use what is already in weft."* Adopt `PanelHeader`, delete `weft-board-head`; the larger board title, if wanted, is a size variant.

**Decision (D10) — comment on this line to record the call.**

---

### D11 · Search + reply — vs `Input` / `Textarea`

![Search + reply — vs `Input` / `Textarea`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** **These are not real controls.** The template ships display-only `div`s inherited from the static mock: no focus ring, no typing, no accessible role. The left column shows the working controls that already exist.

**Recommendation.** Replace both with `Input` and `Textarea`. Not optional — this is a defect, not a variant.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — as recommended.** *"Yes agree fix the defect."* Restores focus-visible, keyboard entry and accessible roles the static-mock markup never had.

**Decision (D11) — comment on this line to record the call.**

