## Group C — genuinely novel (decide: promote to Weft, or keep template-local)

### D12 · Urgency-toned tier group — `weft-board-tier`

![Urgency-toned tier group — `weft-board-tier`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** Weft can group (`SignalGroupCollapsible`) and can tone a value (`Badge`, `MetricTile`), but nothing tones a group container by urgency. The left column shows the closest available today — an untoned bordered group. Every operator surface needs this.

**Recommendation.** **Promote to a Weft primitive.** This is the template's actual contribution.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — as recommended.** *"Promote to weft."* New primitive + plain-CSS counterpart, manifest entry with semver, props-snapshot coverage, gallery specimen.

**Decision (D12) — comment on this line to record the call.**

---

### D13 · Standalone status dot — `weft-board-dot`

![Standalone status dot — `weft-board-dot`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** Weft tones text and pill backgrounds but has no bare 7px semantic dot. The nearest thing is a toned `Badge`, which forces a label you may not want.

**Recommendation.** Promote to the component layer as a `Dot` primitive. Cheap win.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — as recommended.** *"Promote to weft."* Unblocks the D2 `StatRow` variant, which needs exactly this in its leading slot.

**Decision (D13) — comment on this line to record the call.**

---

### D14 · Copyable reference row — `weft-board-drawer-ref`

![Copyable reference row — `weft-board-drawer-ref`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** An ellipsised canonical id with an inline Copy control. The closest assembly today is a `SourcePill` plus a small button, which neither truncates nor shares a frame.

**Recommendation.** Promote. Recurs anywhere a ccore id surfaces.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — as recommended.** *"Promote to weft."* The one promotion carrying behaviour rather than styling: owns truncation plus a clipboard action, so it needs a copy-success affordance and an accessible name.

**Decision (D14) — comment on this line to record the call.**

---

### D15 · Provenance evidence chips — `weft-board-evidence`

![Provenance evidence chips — `weft-board-evidence`](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Evidence.** Visually a toned outline chip Weft already has. What is genuinely introduced is the meaning: a fixed vocabulary for why a row is present (direct id / alias match / trace link), plus the rule that absent evidence renders no chip at all.

**Recommendation.** Build the visual on `Badge`; keep the provenance vocabulary and the never-invent rule as template doctrine, not a component.

**DECIDED 2026-07-29 (Katie) — as recommended.** *"Yes I agree with the recommendation."* Chip built on `Badge`; the provenance vocabulary and never-invent rule stay doctrine, keeping the rule enforceable in review without freezing it into a prop.

**Decision (D15) — comment on this line to record the call.**

